    "old": "<img width=\"760\" class=\"internal\" alt=\"Bookkeeping flow for one glucose. Glycolysis in the cytosol gives 2 pyruvate, 2 ATP and 2 NADH. The two cytosolic NADH enter the mitochondrion through the malate&ndash;aspartate shuttle (worth 5 ATP) or the glycerol-3-phosphate shuttle (worth 3 ATP). Pyruvate dehydrogenase gives 2 acetyl-CoA and 2 NADH. Two turns of the citric acid cycle give 6 NADH, 2 FADH2 and 2 GTP. All NADH and FADH2 go to the electron transport chain, which makes 2.5 ATP per NADH and 1.5 ATP per FADH2. The total is 32 ATP with the malate&ndash;aspartate shuttle or 30 with the glycerol-3-phosphate shuttle.\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;\" src=\"/@api/deki/files/512775/fig-p597204-yield-flow.svg\" fileid=\"512775\" />",
